{
  "id": "urn:visionflow:page:b9ea829e77bc4d85b88adf164f945743e12f315d508621a7c41264c75cf61077",
  "title": "Blackboard Pattern",
  "slug": "blackboard-pattern",
  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:blackboard-pattern",
  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "A coordination architecture in which multiple specialised agents collaborate not by messaging each other directly but by reading from and writing to a shared, structured workspace \u2014 the blackboard. Each agent watches the blackboard for a state it can act on, contributes its partial result back to the shared space, and lets other agents build on that contribution in turn, so a solution accretes incrementally through many opportunistic updates rather than through a fixed pipeline. The pattern decouples the collaborators from one another: an agent needs to understand only the blackboard's contents, not the identity, order, or availability of its peers.",
